# Documentation Guidelines

Documentation must describe actual intended or implemented behavior.

Do not document speculative behavior as implemented behavior.

## Specification Documents

The project may maintain:

spec/requirements.md
spec/architecture.md
spec/data-model.md
spec/api-contract.md
spec/state-machine.md
spec/ui-flow.md
spec/test-strategy.md
spec/decisions.md
spec/traceability.md

Only create artifacts that are relevant to the project.

## Change Synchronization

When changing behavior, determine whether the following need updates:

- requirements
- architecture
- data model
- API contract
- state machine
- UI flow
- test strategy
- decisions
- traceability

Do not leave specifications knowingly inconsistent with implementation.

## Documentation Quality

Prefer concise, precise documentation.

Use diagrams when they communicate relationships or flows better
than prose.

Avoid documenting obvious implementation details that provide
no long-term value.

## Decisions

Important architectural decisions should be recorded in:

spec/decisions.md

Include:

- context
- decision
- alternatives considered
- consequences
